      "title": "General Troubleshooting Guide: Performance, Latency, and Timeout Issues",
      "content_summary": "Comprehensive overview of common causes for system latency, HTTP 504 errors, and timeout issues, including database contention and capacity limits.",
      "content_body": "When users report slow responses or HTTP 504 errors, first check infrastructure metrics for CPU spikes or memory saturation, as capacity limitations are frequent culprits. Investigate database logs for long-running queries or lock contention, which often delay report generation and batch jobs. If the issue is isolated to specific third-party integrations, verify their status pages to rule out external service failures. For persistent latency not tied to clear resource bottlenecks, coordinate with the vendor for deeper infrastructure analysis or optimization. Temporary workarounds, such as adjusting timeout thresholds or scheduling heavy jobs off-peak, may be necessary while root causes are addressed."
